html:
{#- Maintenance Record Print — the customer's service report (Sapphire Maintenance Record).

    The chrome is the print design system's (print_style, reached through the ps_* Jinja
    globals registered in hooks.py): the Service pillar's stripe, the wordmark with our
    contact details, the display-face title, ruled tables. This template composes only
    the report: who, where, what the water read on arrival, what was done, what was
    checked, what was used, and who signed — the order the visit is worked in. Print-safe CSS only — no flex, no grid — because the
    PDF backends on this host cannot lay them out (docs/pdf-generation.md).

    Labor hours are deliberately NOT printed. The portal view shows them only when the
    Sales Order's custom_display_labor_hours is set, and this PDF is what
    api/maintenance_workflow.py emails to the customer on finalize.

    Per Site Visit records (a contract covering several water features in one form)
    have no header serial — child rows are tagged with their feature instead, so the
    tables grow a Water Feature column.

    v1.597.0 (Lisa's review of the first report, 2026-10-12): water features print by
    name, not ID; the customer block carries the contract with the visit's calendar year
    and the PRJ number; the water chemistry gets a chart per reading over recent visits;
    the technician's "fountain as we left it" photo prints at the end. All of it comes
    from maintenance_report(doc) (sapphire_maintenance/visit_report.py), which the
    sandbox cannot compute and which never raises: a part that fails is left out.

    v1.598.0: a cleaning task is Done, N/A (not needed on this visit, such as a winter-only
    check in October) or Not done, and its note says why. Lisa, on the Myers report: "It
    only states that one cartridge wasn't cleaned out; why wasn't it?"

    v1.600.0: Follow-ups and Parts Needed, what the technician found the site needs after
    today and who on site was told. Each becomes a tracked Maintenance Follow-Up when the
    visit is approved. -#}
{{ ps_page_open("service") }}
{%- set per_site = doc.maintenance_contract and not doc.serial_no -%}
{%- set mr = maintenance_report(doc) -%}
{%- set customer_name = (frappe.db.get_value("Customer", doc.customer, "customer_name") if doc.customer else "") or doc.customer or "" -%}
{%- set technician_name = (frappe.db.get_value("User", doc.technician, "full_name") if doc.technician else "") or doc.technician or "" -%}
{%- set project_name = (frappe.db.get_value("Project", doc.project, "project_name") if doc.project else "") or doc.project or "" -%}
{%- set meta -%}
<span style="{{ ps_style("strong") }}">{{ doc.name }}</span><br>{{ frappe.format(doc.visit_date or doc.scheduled_visit_date or doc.creation, {"fieldtype": "Date"}) }}{% if doc.workflow_state %}<br>{{ doc.workflow_state | e }}{% endif %}
{%- endset -%}
{{ ps_letterhead("service", "MAINTENANCE VISIT REPORT", "Maintenance Visit Report", meta) }}
{{ ps_facts_open() }}
{%- set contract_html = (mr.contract_line | e) if mr.contract_line else (project_name | e) -%}
{%- set feature_html = (mr.feature_lines | map("e") | join("<br>")) if mr.feature_lines else ((doc.serial_no | e) if doc.serial_no else "Site visit") -%}
{{ ps_fact("CUSTOMER", (customer_name | e) ~ ("<br>" ~ contract_html if contract_html else "") ~ ("<br>Project " ~ (doc.project | e) if doc.project else "")) }}
{{ ps_fact("WATER FEATURE", feature_html ~ ("<br>Contract " ~ (doc.maintenance_contract | e) if doc.maintenance_contract else "") ~ ("<br>" ~ (doc.visit_label | e) if doc.visit_label else "")) }}
{{ ps_fact("TECHNICIAN", (technician_name | e) ~ ("<br>Sapphire Fountains" if technician_name else "")) }}
{{ ps_facts_close() }}

{%- if doc.chemistry_readings %}
{{ ps_section_title("Water Chemistry") }}
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
  <thead style="display:table-header-group;">
    <tr>
      {%- if per_site %}<th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Water Feature</th>{% endif %}
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Reading</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service", true) }}">Value</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Target range</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Result</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in doc.chemistry_readings %}
    <tr style="page-break-inside:avoid;">
      {%- if per_site %}<td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (mr.features.get(row.serial_no) or row.serial_no or "") | e }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.reading or "") | e }}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td(true) }}">{% if row.out_of_range %}<span style="{{ ps_style("fail") }}">{{ row.reading_value }} {{ (row.uom or "") | e }}</span>{% else %}{{ row.reading_value }} {{ (row.uom or "") | e }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ row.min_value }}&ndash;{{ row.max_value }} {{ (row.uom or "") | e }}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{% if row.out_of_range %}<span style="{{ ps_style("fail") }}">Out of range</span>{% else %}In range{% endif %}{% if row.notes %} &middot; {{ row.notes | e }}{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{%- if mr.charts %}
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-top:10px; page-break-inside:avoid;">
  <tr>
    {%- for chart in mr.charts %}
    <td style="width:50%; padding:4px 0; vertical-align:top;">{{ chart }}</td>
    {%- if loop.index is divisibleby 2 and not loop.last %}</tr><tr>{% endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- if mr.charts | length is odd %}<td style="width:50%;"></td>{% endif %}
  </tr>
</table>
<div style="font-size:10.5px;">Recent visits to this site. The shaded band is the target range; red points were out of range.</div>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if doc.cleaning_tasks %}
{{ ps_section_title("Cleaning &amp; Service Tasks") }}
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
  <thead style="display:table-header-group;">
    <tr>
      {%- if per_site %}<th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Water Feature</th>{% endif %}
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Task</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Status</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Notes</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in doc.cleaning_tasks %}
    <tr style="page-break-inside:avoid;">
      {%- if per_site %}<td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (mr.features.get(row.serial_no) or row.serial_no or "") | e }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.task or "") | e }}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{% if row.is_done %}<span style="{{ ps_style("strong") }}">Done</span>{% elif row.not_applicable %}N/A{% else %}Not done{% endif %}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.notes or "") | e }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{%- endif %}

{%- if doc.maintenance_results %}
{{ ps_section_title("Checklist Results") }}
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
  <thead style="display:table-header-group;">
    <tr>
      {%- if per_site %}<th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Water Feature</th>{% endif %}
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Item</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Status</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Notes</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in doc.maintenance_results %}
    <tr style="page-break-inside:avoid;">
      {%- if per_site %}<td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (mr.features.get(row.serial_no) or row.serial_no or "") | e }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.question or "") | e }}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{% if row.selection == "Fail" %}<span style="{{ ps_style("fail") }}">Fail</span>{% else %}<span style="{{ ps_style("strong") }}">{{ (row.selection or "") | e }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.answer or "") | e }}{% if row.selection == "Other" and row.other_details %} &mdash; {{ row.other_details | e }}{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{%- endif %}

{%- set used = [] -%}
{%- for row in doc.consumables or [] %}{% if row.qty %}{% set _ = used.append(row) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- if used %}
{{ ps_section_title("Consumables Used") }}
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
  <thead style="display:table-header-group;">
    <tr>
      {%- if per_site %}<th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Water Feature</th>{% endif %}
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Item</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service", true) }}">Quantity</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in used %}
    <tr style="page-break-inside:avoid;">
      {%- if per_site %}<td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (mr.features.get(row.serial_no) or row.serial_no or "") | e }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.item_name or row.item or "") | e }}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td(true) }}">{{ row.qty }} {{ (row.uom or "") | e }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{%- endif %}

{%- if doc.visit_notes %}
{{ ps_section_title("Visit Notes") }}
<div style="font-size:12.5px; white-space:pre-wrap;">{{ doc.visit_notes | e }}</div>
{%- endif %}

{%- if doc.follow_ups %}
{{ ps_section_title("Follow-ups and Parts Needed") }}
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;">
  <thead style="display:table-header-group;">
    <tr>
      {%- if per_site %}<th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Water Feature</th>{% endif %}
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">What Is Needed</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Part</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service", true) }}">Qty</th>
      <th style="{{ ps_th("service") }}">Told On Site</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in doc.follow_ups %}
    <tr style="page-break-inside:avoid;">
      {%- if per_site %}<td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (mr.features.get(row.serial_no) or row.serial_no or "Whole site") | e }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }} white-space:pre-wrap;">{{ (row.description or "") | e }}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{% if row.item %}{{ (frappe.db.get_value("Item", row.item, "item_name") or row.item) | e }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td(true) }}">{% if row.qty %}{{ row.qty }}{% endif %}</td>
      <td style="{{ ps_td() }}">{{ (row.told or "") | e }}</td>
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{%- endif %}

{%- if mr.fountain_photo %}
{{ ps_section_title("The Fountain As We Left It") }}
<div style="page-break-inside:avoid;"><img src="{{ mr.fountain_photo | e }}" alt="The fountain as we left it" style="display:block; max-width:100%; max-height:320px;"></div>
{%- endif %}

<div style="display:table; width:100%; margin-top:20px; page-break-inside:avoid;">
  <div style="display:table-cell; width:50%; vertical-align:bottom; padding-right:32px;">
    <div style="{{ ps_style("label") }}">CLIENT SIGN-OFF</div>
    {%- if doc.client_sign_off %}
    <img src="{{ doc.client_sign_off }}" alt="Client signature" style="display:block; max-height:56px; margin-top:4px;">
    {%- else %}
    <div style="height:44px;"></div>
    {%- endif %}
    <div style="border-top:1px solid #00263e; padding-top:4px; font-size:11px;">{% if doc.client_sign_off %}Digitally captured on site{% else %}Not signed on site{% endif %}</div>
  </div>
  <div style="display:table-cell; width:50%; vertical-align:bottom;">
    <div style="{{ ps_style("label") }}">TECHNICIAN</div>
    <div style="height:44px;"></div>
    <div style="border-top:1px solid #00263e; padding-top:4px; font-size:11px;">{{ technician_name | e }}{% if technician_name %} &middot; {% endif %}Sapphire Fountains</div>
  </div>
</div>
{{ ps_page_close("service") }}

css:
/* Sapphire Fountains contract styling — the print design system's look
   (docs/print-design-system.md) applied to the agreements.

   Every rule is scoped under .contract-doc on purpose: this stylesheet is
   published document-wide by public/js/project_enhancements/contract_viewer.js
   and by the /contract-sign page, and an unscoped rule would restyle the desk
   (or the portal) around the agreement.

   This record is the single source of truth for how a contract looks. The desk
   print, the on-screen viewer, the public signing page and the executed PDF
   emailed after signing all read it — see project_contract._contract_css. The
   letterhead (pillar stripe, wordmark, eyebrow) and the @font-face for the
   display face are emitted by contract_style.letterhead_html(), OUTSIDE the
   signed snapshot, so they reach every contract including those signed before
   they existed. */

.contract-doc { font-family: Lato, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 1.45; color: #363636; }
.contract-doc p { margin: 5px 0; text-align: justify; }

/* Letterhead: built by project_enhancements/contract_style.py, first page only. */
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead { margin: 0 0 14px; page-break-after: avoid; }
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead svg { width: 190px; height: auto; }
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead-name { font-family: 'Big Noodle Titling', 'Arial Narrow', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20pt; color: #00263e; }
.contract-doc .ct-eyebrow { font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 10px; }

/* The document title block, targeted by POSITION rather than by tag. The eight
   shipped templates disagree about tags: <h3> opens the document in six of them
   but is a mid-document section head in the employee-contractor agreement and
   the NDA. So the title is "the <h3> immediately after the letterhead", and its
   subtitle/company/address lines are the run of <p> after that (four is the
   longest run any shipped template has). The chain is inert for the architect
   agreement and the NDA, which open with no title block at all. */
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead + h3 { font-family: 'Big Noodle Titling', 'Arial Narrow', Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 24pt; line-height: 1; text-align: center; color: #00263e; border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 4px 0 4px; }
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead + h3 + p,
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead + h3 + p + p,
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead + h3 + p + p + p,
.contract-doc .ct-letterhead + h3 + p + p + p + p { text-align: center; font-size: 9.5pt; color: #363636; margin: 1px 0; }

/* Numbered section headings: the display face in bahama-blue against the body.
   No rule and no box — the design system separates a heading with weight and
   space, never a border. */
.contract-doc h1 { font-family: 'Big Noodle Titling', 'Arial Narrow', Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1; color: #00609c; text-align: left; border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 16px 0 7px; page-break-after: avoid; }
.contract-doc h2 { font-family: Lato, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10.5pt; font-weight: 700; color: #00263e; margin: 12px 0 5px; page-break-after: avoid; }
.contract-doc h3 { font-family: Lato, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: 700; color: #00263e; margin: 12px 0 6px; page-break-after: avoid; }

/* Tables. The templates write label cells as <td><b>Label:</b></td> and never
   use <th>, so the first column is set in bahama-blue to read as the label
   column — a rule, not a tint, is what separates cells. */
.contract-doc table.ct-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 8px 0; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.contract-doc table.ct-table td { border: 1px solid #dadbdd; padding: 5px 7px; vertical-align: top; font-size: 10pt; }
.contract-doc table.ct-table td:first-child { color: #00609c; }

.contract-doc .ct-blank { display: inline-block; border-bottom: 1px solid #00263e; min-height: 1em; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; }
.contract-doc .ct-cb { font-size: 12pt; color: #00263e; }

/* Signature ink stays black. It is evidence, not decoration. */
.contract-doc .ct-sig { max-height: 60px; vertical-align: bottom; }
.contract-doc .ct-sig-typed { font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-style: italic; font-size: 15pt; color: #000; }

/* Client initials beside a clause (the templates' initial() helper). A blank box on paper and
   in every unsigned render; the client's drawn initials, in place, once signed. */
.contract-doc .ct-initial { display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 6px; white-space: nowrap; }
.contract-doc .ct-initial-box { display: inline-block; width: 52px; height: 22px; border: 1px solid #00263e; border-radius: 3px; vertical-align: middle; }
.contract-doc .ct-initial-label { font-size: 7.5pt; color: #6b7280; margin-left: 4px; vertical-align: middle; }
.contract-doc .ct-initial-img { max-height: 28px; max-width: 80px; vertical-align: middle; border-bottom: 1px solid #00263e; }

/* "What you are agreeing to, in short" (project_enhancements/contract_summary.py): the client's own
   terms in plain words, after the title. A tinted card so it reads as a guide, not a clause. */
.contract-doc .ct-summary { border: 1px solid #00609c; border-radius: 6px; background: #f2f7fb; padding: 8px 14px 6px; margin: 12px 0 16px; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.contract-doc .ct-summary h2 { margin: 2px 0 6px; color: #00263e; }
.contract-doc .ct-summary ul { margin: 0 0 4px; padding-left: 18px; }
.contract-doc .ct-summary li { margin: 3px 0; text-align: left; }
.contract-doc .ct-summary-note { font-size: 9pt; font-style: italic; color: #4b5563; text-align: left; }
.contract-doc .ct-certificate { margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 2px solid #00263e; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.contract-doc .ct-certificate h1 { font-size: 12pt; border: 0; padding: 0; text-align: center; }

/* The running footer is for paper only. frappe.utils.pdf lifts #footer-html out
   of the document and renders it as wkhtmltopdf's --footer-html; in that
   standalone render nothing has a .contract-doc ancestor, so this rule stops
   applying and the footer appears exactly where it should. On every other
   surface the div is still in the body, and hidden. */
.contract-doc #footer-html { display: none; }
